# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit the real .env file.
# Expo automatically loads EXPO_PUBLIC_* vars — these are bundled into the client, so nothing
# secret belongs here (see docs/PRODUCT_AND_COMPLIANCE.md §7/§15).

# Optional. Defaults handle both simulators automatically (10.0.2.2 for the Android emulator,
# localhost for iOS Simulator — see src/api/config.ts). Set this only for a physical device on
# the same network as the backend (your machine's LAN IP), or a staging/prod API URL.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.23:3000

# A Google Cloud OAuth Web client id (public identifier, not a secret) — required for Google
# Sign-In to actually work. Left unset/placeholder, the sign-in button fails fast with a clear
# "not configured" message instead of attempting a native OAuth handshake with a bogus id.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-google-oauth-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
